r's swimming flag\" in some maps. Let me recall the SMB RAM map (from doppelganger):\n  - $0700 = Player_XSpeed\n  - $0701 = Player_YSpeed?\n  - $0704 = Player swimming flag? \n  - $0714 = Crouching flag?\n  - $0770 = GameMode\n  - $0756 = PlayerPowerUp\nHmm.\n\nActually the well-known SMB RAM map:\n$0700 Player_XSpeed\n$0701 Player_YSpeed... not sure.\n\nLet me recall \"CrouchingFlag\" address. In the SMB disassembly (smbdis), variables:\n- `CrouchingFlag = $0714`? \n- `SwimmingFlag = $0704`?\nI have vague memory that `$0704` is `Player_IsDucking`? Not sure.\n\nThe task wants discovery by differential search. Let's do it properly.\n\nLet me start. First take screenshot / check state.\n\nLet's get current game state and make big Mario.\n\nNote: runtime says bridge not connected but tools should work.\n\nLet me do parallel: screenshot + get_rom_info? Not needed. Let's screenshot and pause.\n\nActually the screenshot earlier showed the 1-1 starting screen with Mario on the hill. TIME 260 suggests some time has passed (start 400?). Hmm, TIME 260, Mario standing on hill. Could be fine.\n\nWait, actually screenshot showed small Mario standing on ground near a hill, with ? block at right. The camera likely at 0. Good, this is the start of 1-1.\n\nLet's proceed:\n1. pause_emulator\n2. write $0756=1, $0754=0\n3. step 3 frames, screenshot to confirm big.\n\nThen save_state.\n\nLet's go."}
