tial experiment in 2-2. First save state.\n\nLet me do:\n- save_state slot 1\n- snapshot w_idle0\n- play_input [] 40\n- snapshot w_idle1\n- diff increased name wi (control)\n\nThen:\n- play_input [{a}] 40  → but note: 40 frames of A. Then snapshot w_a.\n- diff from wi filter increased name wa — candidates that moved both times.\n\nHmm, but if swim flag is \"in water\" constant, it won't appear. Then I need the level-comparison method.\n\nLet me just try. Actually, wait: better experiment for \"swims\": in water, Mario on the floor is \"standing\"; if I hold A he swims (kick animation). The flag might toggle 0/1 with the stroke.\n\nLet me first do the control to see baseline. Actually, I can combine: snapshot w0; play_input [{none,40}] snapshot w1; diff. This shows what changes while idle in water (timer, RNG, sinking y).\n\nThen snapshot w2 after play_input [{a,40}] and diff from w1.\n\nLet me go."}
