{"type":"text","text":"Both flags are found, proven by watching, and recorded/promoted.\n\n## Results\n\n### 1. Big-Mario crouch flag — `$0714`\n- **Encoding:** `0` = not crouching, `4` = crouching. It isn't a clean 1 — the ducking code stores the Down direction bit itself: `$B330` does `LDA $1D / BNE / LDA $0B / AND #$04 / STA $0714`, so nonzero = crouching.\n- **Search:** with Mario made big (`$0756=1,$0754=0`), three hold-Down/release cycles narrowed the \"increased\" diff from 26 to 20 survivors; `$0714` went 0→4 on each hold and back to 0 on release.\n- **Control:** the same Down hold with *small* Mario left `$0714` at 0 (raw button bytes `$000B/$06FC/$074A` still showed the Down bit), so it is not an input mirror.\n- **Watch proof (as asked):** `play_input [{none,10},{down,40},{none,30},{down,30}]`, watching `$0714` every 2 frames → `0,0,0,0,0, 4,4,… (all 20 held frames), 0,…,0 (released), 4,… (second hold)`.\n- **Code:** `$B644` skips the walk animation when it's set; `$BD57` uses it to pick the short crouch hitbox.\n\n### 2. Swimming flag — `$0704`\n- **Encoding:** `1` = water area / Mario is swimming, `0` = everywhere else. It's a per-area flag, set once for the whole level.\n- **Search:** World 2-2 reached via title-screen writes `$075F=1,$075C=1,$0760=2` + Start. A in water changed `$0706/$0707/$0708` too, but a land jump gave the identical `1/1/176`, so those are jump/swim force params, not the flag. Comparing the `$0700-$071F` page between 1-1 (0) and 2-2 (1) isolated `$0704`.\n- **Watch proof (as asked):** in 2-2, `play_input [{a,40},{right,80},{right+a,80}]`, sampling `$0704` every 4 frames → **1 for all 50 samples** while swimming. The same byte read 0 in World 1-1 and in the World 1-2 area (`$074E=1`).\n- **Code:** area/player init `$914D-$9153` does `LDA $074E / BNE / INY / STY $0704` (1 iff area type is water); player physics reads it at `$B393` and `$B48F` to switch to swim movement. (For contrast, the other water-vs-land candidate `$0701` is just a `ROL`'d fixed-point speed fraction.)\n\nBoth are recorded with `source: \"differential search\"` (notes include the disassembly corroboration) and promoted — the mapping file now has 32 addresses."}
